assistant: Subject: convert cents to dollars for newer vendor API versions

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 now sends `price` in cents, under the same field name. Version 2026-01-01, the one in the published spec, sent dollars. `search_products` passed the value through unchanged, so a 1199 USD laptop showed up as 119900. The fix reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides `price` by 100 when the version is newer than 2026-01-01. If the header is missing, it treats the response as the old version, so the v1 fixtures produce exactly the same output as before. Typecheck, lint and all 13 tests pass. Two assumptions are unconfirmed: the spec and recorded traces don't say which version introduced cents, so the cutoff "anything after 2026-01-01" is my guess. `get_product` reads the same field and is probably affected too, but I left it alone because there is no recorded v2 traffic for it.

